Subject: Cantor Recursive Machine Schema Data Design

@ [design_uuid] 45f8bc8f-0c81-4884-9a50-996139dd81e1

& [RecursiveDefinitionAccount] is inspectable
  + type_name
  + document_id
  + local_definition_pointer
  + direct_local_reference_targets
  + self_recursive boolean
  + strongly_connected_component members
  + schema_fingerprint
  + semantic_residual_ids

& [TraversalState] is finite
  + pending definition identities in deterministic lexical order
  + visited definition identities
  + active path identities for cycle classification
  + counters for definitions, references, properties, alternatives, depth, and bytes
  + typed fault with limit, observed count, active path, and safe residual on failure

& [Residuals] bind layers
  + RMS-R01 serde JSON container recursion limit remains active
  + RMS-R02 ProcedureBounds.maximum_call_depth is positive and no greater than 64
  + RMS-R03 ProcedureType recursion is validated with decrementing depth
  + RMS-R04 ProcedureValue recursion is validated with decrementing depth
  + RMS-R05 value bytes, text, collection items, and map entries remain core-enforced
  + RMS-R06 schema validation never substitutes for authority admission

& [ConformanceCorpus] is boundary directed
  + shallow scalar and one-level recursive values
  + nested list, map, record, tagged union, and recursive type cases
  + semantic depth 63, 64, and 65 after constructing complete safe fixtures
  + JSON container depths immediately below and above the active serde boundary
  + unresolved local reference and every forbidden external-reference shape
  + self-cycle traversal repeats and counter-exhaustion cases

